    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression and live character vitals, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.8 — Vitals against the real Build 42 API[/h1]\n[b]Fixed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]1.7 read the character through Build 41 accessors that Build 42 had moved. Every one raised, was swallowed by the collector's own error guard, and returned a default — so the dashboard showed every body part at 100% with no wounds, a flat 37°C, and no moodles, while the server log filled with roughly a hundred stack traces per heartbeat, per player.\n[*]Body parts are now addressed by BodyPartType instead of by name, which is what BodyDamage has always required. The part list is read out of the enum rather than hardcoded, so it cannot drift from the game again — and it no longer claims a \"Torso\", which Build 42 splits into Torso_Upper and Torso_Lower.\n[*]Wounds are assembled from the real BodyPart flags — bitten, scratched, deep wound, cut, burnt, fracture, infection — with severity taken from what the part has been reduced to, and treatment from whether it is bandaged or stitched.\n[*]Body temperature now comes from the thermoregulator's per-part thermal nodes. BodyDamage exposes no temperature accessors at all.\n[*]Moodles are read through Stats.get(CharacterStat), replacing the getters Build 42 removed.\n[*]Weapon attachments use getAttachmentsProvided, and sharpness is reported as a proportion of the weapon's own maximum rather than as a raw value.\n[/list]\n[b]Removed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]The per-body-part bite and scratch protection panel. PZ exposes defence on the garment only — there is no accessor for what a body part ends up protected by, and the game's own UI never shows one. The clothing panel carries both figures per garment instead.\n[*]The quickload hotbar panel and the favourite weapon field. Neither has any API behind it on a character.\n[/list]\n[b]Notes[/b]\nPanels that never worked are gone rather than left drawing plausible defaults, so a server on 1.7 is now treated by the web dashboard as not having the feature at all — showing fabricated vitals is worse than showing none. Upgrade both the mod and the panel together."
}
